;; What the model reads of each tool brainyard/hookbox.clj defines: its description,
;; by tool id (brainyard.tool-words, byj-2e8.5). Read by the model, so a
;; resource (RFC-001).
{"hook$events"
  "List the agent events a hook can observe, with their payload keys."
 "hook$validate"
  "Check a user hook definition (same args as hook$create, all optional but body) without saving it; with `sample`, run the body on that sample event."
 "hook$list"
  "List the registered hooks, built-in and user."
 "hook$read"
  "Read a user hook's definition, including its Tool Lisp body."
 "hook$delete"
  "Delete a user hook: unregister it and remove its files."}
